obs Proved the verbs by the algebra they must obey rather than a hand-checked index formula: rotate_quarter four times = identity byte-for-byte, rotate_quarter(2) = flip_h(flip_v), each mirror its own inverse, rotate_quarter(k) = k single turns; a 90 turn swaps dims and a concrete clockwise corner (top-left to top-right) pins direction; a rotated image still re-encodes and round-trips as an open image. This catches an index bug regardless of the exact arithmetic.
obs Used a non-square 3x5 tagged image so a width/height swap is visible and a turn can never masquerade as a transpose or a no-op.
